Looking at the code in `repair.go`, I can see the bug in the `Contains` function. The issue is on line 4:

```go
for i := 0; i < len(xs)-1; i++ {
```

This loop condition excludes the last element because it uses `len(xs)-1` as the upper bound. The function should check all elements including the last one, so the condition should be `i < len(xs)`.

Let me fix this bug:
